#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# annulus

#% text
# `annulus(c, [r0, r1])` is the ring between the circles of radii `r0` and `r1` about `c`: a primitive of graphics and a region.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `annulus()` is `annulus([0, 0], [1/2, 1])`, `annulus(c)` the ring of radii 1/2 and 1 about `c`, and `annulus(r)` the ring between the circles of radii `r/2` and `r` about the origin.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
graphics([orange, annulus([0, 0], [1, 2])])
#% output
#= image("annulus.files/annulus-1.svgz")

#% cell
region_measure(annulus([0, 0], [1, 2]))
#% output
#= 3*pi

#% cell
annulus()
#% output
#= annulus([0, 0], [1/2, 1])

#% cell
region_member(annulus(), [3/4, 0])
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_measure`
